WEBVTT

1
00:00:47.652 --> 00:00:50.969
Violence filled the streets as the Mayor
declared marshall law today.

2
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.233
Naming Detroit as the most
dangerous city in America.

3
00:00:55.062 --> 00:00:58.348
The housing project has been
sealed off in the rest of the city.

4
00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.611
The homicide rate is
at the highest in 40 years.

5
00:01:03.823 --> 00:01:08.969
Community active project known as
Brick Mansions will become a ghost town.

6
00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:12.158
More protesting of the construction
of the 44 foot wall

7
00:01:12.201 --> 00:01:15.454
that will separate Brick Mansions
from the rest of the city.

8
00:01:16.592 --> 00:01:20.706
These checkpoints control all the
people in and out of Brick Mansions.

9
00:01:24.013 --> 00:01:25.916
Gentleman...

10
00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:31.178
This development is a beacon
of light in our dark city.

11
00:01:31.209 --> 00:01:34.427
Eco friendly residences,
exclusive shops and offices

12
00:01:34.437 --> 00:01:41.528
all situated on 20 acres of the most
valuable property that the city owns.

13
00:01:41.529 --> 00:01:43.779
Now, with your cooperation
and your backing,

14
00:01:43.789 --> 00:01:46.944
we're gonna restore
Detroit to it's former glory.

15
00:01:46.986 --> 00:01:48.965
Mr. Mayor.

16
00:01:48.996 --> 00:01:53.120
This land is currently the
Brick Mansions housing project.

17
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.088
In order for this to go up,
that has to come down.

18
00:01:58.244 --> 00:02:02.368
Yes, what is it do you envision
for the people currently living there?

19
00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:08.762
Well, as your Mayor I can assure you
that all the people of this fine city

20
00:02:08.772 --> 00:02:10.918
will be taken care of.

21
00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.958
Gentleman, to the future.

22
00:02:52.376 --> 00:02:53.553
- Yo, yo, yo.
- What's up killer?

23
00:02:53.563 --> 00:02:55.615
Check that shit out.

24
00:03:03.748 --> 00:03:05.883
What's cooking my brothers?

25
00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:08.945
Yeah, you best keep on rolling dawg.

26
00:03:08.987 --> 00:03:13.111
- What are you doing here K2?
- Come on now, why the hate?

27
00:03:16.287 --> 00:03:20.411
I'm looking for Lino.
He's got something for me.

28
00:03:23.827 --> 00:03:26.639
- Lino ain't here.
- Nah.

29
00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.753
I'm gonna bet Lino's up
there right now.

30
00:03:28.794 --> 00:03:31.085
He thinks he can change the ghetto
20 kilos at a time.

31
00:03:31.096 --> 00:03:35.084
Bet your ass ain't gonna find out.

32
00:03:40.333 --> 00:03:41.468
I'm gonna leave you my number.

33
00:03:41.479 --> 00:03:45.509
And when Mr. Clean comes back,
you tell him to give me a call.

34
00:03:49.716 --> 00:03:51.820
Come on, K2.

35
00:03:54.965 --> 00:03:59.089
Fill them up.

36
00:04:23.218 --> 00:04:25.196
- Y'all know where Lino stay at?
- Yes.

37
00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:27.134
Come on.

38
00:04:36.517 --> 00:04:38.735
- Where?
- Right, right.

39
00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.932
Lino.

40
00:04:45.838 --> 00:04:48.118
At the end of that hall, left door!

41
00:04:48.129 --> 00:04:51.003
I'm gonna get you.

42
00:05:00.563 --> 00:05:02.709
Knock this damn door down.

43
00:05:02.761 --> 00:05:04.833
On my count.

44
00:05:04.843 --> 00:05:07.936
One, two...

45
00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:19.361
Catch that little bitch!

46
00:05:19.371 --> 00:05:22.454
Lock this piece of shit building down!

47
00:05:37.887 --> 00:05:41.001
- She is cute, I know.
- She's got a great ass, man.

48
00:05:44.146 --> 00:05:46.250
- Hi kids.
- Hey Lino.

49
00:06:05.099 --> 00:06:07.108
Ah, hell no.

50
00:06:07.109 --> 00:06:09.255
- Tremaine's gonna slice y'all.
- What do we do?

51
00:06:09.296 --> 00:06:11.275
Who's we?

52
00:06:12.327 --> 00:06:15.441
I'm gonna kill this motherfucker!

53
00:06:16.701 --> 00:06:18.711
Get him!

54
00:06:38.529 --> 00:06:40.570
He's on the roof!

55
00:07:22.059 --> 00:07:24.382
What's going on man?

56
00:08:48.621 --> 00:08:52.850
♪ I can't see where you comin' from ♪

57
00:08:52.891 --> 00:08:57.057
♪ But I know just what you runnin' from ♪

58
00:08:57.869 --> 00:09:02.169
♪ And what matters ain't the
who's baddest but ♪

59
00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:05.158
♪ The ones who stop you fallin'
from your ladde baby ♪

60
00:09:05.159 --> 00:09:07.273
Damien, you forgot me.

61
00:09:07.283 --> 00:09:09.533
No, I'm just throwing some
overtime at work.

62
00:09:11.418 --> 00:09:15.646
♪ When I love you like the way I love you ♪

63
00:09:17.708 --> 00:09:18.874
How much do you need?

64
00:09:18.926 --> 00:09:20.935
Okay, well...

65
00:09:20.936 --> 00:09:22.884
I will see what we can do.

66
00:09:22.915 --> 00:09:27.039
But never call my cellular phone again.

67
00:09:28.164 --> 00:09:30.278
Who give him my number?

68
00:09:34.318 --> 00:09:37.432
Mr. George, I'm sorry,
I didn't know.

69
00:09:39.598 --> 00:09:41.608
Where was I?

70
00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:44.701
- K2.
- K2.

71
00:09:44.743 --> 00:09:48.929
Loses a package. Needs another 20
before Tremaine flips out.

72
00:09:48.981 --> 00:09:52.127
Best part, he wants it delivered.

73
00:09:54.261 --> 00:09:57.282
Guess we have to go to Brick Mansions.

74
00:09:57.323 --> 00:10:01.551
Now, who wants to venture
into that shithole on a Friday night?

75
00:10:01.593 --> 00:10:03.467
I would.

76
00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.664
Think you can handle it?

77
00:10:07.852 --> 00:10:10.726
I am known as a handler.

78
00:10:12.882 --> 00:10:14.090
All right.

79
00:10:53.715 --> 00:10:55.725
You know, my mama
will be turning her grave

80
00:10:55.736 --> 00:10:59.849
if she see me adding this
much hot pepper to her recipe.

81
00:11:00.943 --> 00:11:03.963
Though I appreciate
most of my mother's recipe.

82
00:11:04.005 --> 00:11:06.952
You get the right ingredients.

83
00:11:08.035 --> 00:11:10.388
You can never go wrong.

84
00:11:11.336 --> 00:11:14.355
Which leads us to this morning, K2.

85
00:11:14.356 --> 00:11:18.511
I believe you had the right
ingredients and clear instructions.

86
00:11:18.563 --> 00:11:23.666
Bring back Lino and my 20 kilos
that he jacked from you.

87
00:11:23.843 --> 00:11:29.082
Yet here we are, no Lino, no kilos.

88
00:11:29.957 --> 00:11:32.247
Look, big dawg,
me and Rayzah, you know...

89
00:11:32.248 --> 00:11:36.132
Don't you go blame this
on a woman, dawg.

90
00:11:36.174 --> 00:11:39.402
There's five of my men down.
They become your little shit show.

91
00:11:39.412 --> 00:11:43.672
That's five more souls thats gone.

92
00:11:43.714 --> 00:11:47.671
Should I make six?

93
00:11:47.681 --> 00:11:49.899
Should I make it six?

94
00:11:54.877 --> 00:11:57.231
I pay good money for your services.

95
00:11:58.033 --> 00:12:00.282
I need some good ideas.

96
00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.323
You got any good ideas?

97
00:12:05.333 --> 00:12:08.624
How about you?
Any ideas?

98
00:12:08.634 --> 00:12:11.623
No, sir.

99
00:12:11.655 --> 00:12:14.674
And that's six.
Shall I make it seven?

100
00:12:14.675 --> 00:12:16.789
Hold up, hold up, Lino got a girl.

101
00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.038
Back in the day, he helped her
get out of the hood.

102
00:12:18.049 --> 00:12:21.933
We grab that bitch and
I swear he's gonna come around.

103
00:12:23.016 --> 00:12:26.108
- You know where she's at?
- Yeah, we know where she at.

104
00:12:26.109 --> 00:12:28.255
Don't come back here without her.

105
00:12:28.369 --> 00:12:30.546
Yo, trust me man.

106
00:12:32.535 --> 00:12:34.555
All right.

107
00:12:58.497 --> 00:13:00.715
That's it, George the Greek.

108
00:13:00.726 --> 00:13:02.767
How long you've been
with me now Damien, a year?

109
00:13:02.809 --> 00:13:03.840
Yeah, about that.

110
00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:06.839
It's time for you to see
what we're all about.

111
00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:10.973
Where are you going?
Go park the car in the back.

112
00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:20.554
Cheng, how is it going?

113
00:13:20.565 --> 00:13:24.449
You kill me, Cheng.

114
00:13:24.491 --> 00:13:25.771
Damien, Cheng.
Cheng, Damien.

115
00:13:29.666 --> 00:13:31.843
- You're a man of many talents.
- I try.

116
00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.165
Cheng, you have some change for me?

117
00:13:45.475 --> 00:13:47.350
Cool.

118
00:13:53.848 --> 00:13:56.962
All team,
they've gone underground.

119
00:14:06.251 --> 00:14:08.230
You ever been
to Southeast Asia, Damien?

120
00:14:08.344 --> 00:14:09.480
No, I never been there.

121
00:14:12.437 --> 00:14:13.510
He's found the stash.

122
00:14:13.551 --> 00:14:17.748
Hey, prep me 20 key, it's a rush.

123
00:14:17.832 --> 00:14:20.737
South East Asia planted this drug
by the side of the road

124
00:14:20.748 --> 00:14:22.851
which is why the dope
there is worth shit.

125
00:14:22.903 --> 00:14:26.121
But everytime it crosses a border,
it triples in value.

126
00:14:26.132 --> 00:14:30.016
Used to be that,
by the time it got to the States

127
00:14:30.058 --> 00:14:32.276
there was only so much profit
you can squeeze.

128
00:14:32.391 --> 00:14:34.328
And then, we got Brick Mansions.

129
00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:37.514
Our very own border
and it's less than a mile away.

130
00:14:37.566 --> 00:14:40.617
I went to business school,
the best business school in the world.

131
00:14:40.618 --> 00:14:42.763
4 years, half a million bucks.

132
00:14:44.617 --> 00:14:45.866
You just have to remember one thing.

133
00:14:45.908 --> 00:14:48.928
People pay the most
for what they cannot get.

134
00:14:48.959 --> 00:14:50.094
Can I have that GPS?

135
00:14:51.042 --> 00:14:53.125
The routes are pre programmed.

136
00:14:54.104 --> 00:14:55.208
Don't lose it.

137
00:14:55.249 --> 00:14:57.395
Hey boss, take a look at this.

138
00:15:01.331 --> 00:15:03.508
How the hell did they know we're here?

139
00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:07.580
Now they know we are here.

140
00:15:07.726 --> 00:15:09.798
We weren't suppose to be here.

141
00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:15.890
No one knows we're here,
unless that person is already here.

142
00:15:27.606 --> 00:15:29.646
Damien, you take this.
Take them out.

143
00:15:29.647 --> 00:15:32.604
In the sewers! Let's go!

144
00:15:32.605 --> 00:15:35.698
Go to the marker!

145
00:15:36.875 --> 00:15:38.821
All teams, go!

146
00:15:41.915 --> 00:15:44.060
Give me the phone.

147
00:15:44.071 --> 00:15:45.279
- Put it down!
- The hell are you doing?

148
00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:49.350
Nobody move! Those are my friends
outside, you're all under arrest!

149
00:15:49.351 --> 00:15:52.308
Now I want you all to put your
guns in the tank!

150
00:15:55.578 --> 00:15:57.651
Put it in the tank!

151
00:16:03.878 --> 00:16:05.086
Get down on the ground.

152
00:16:05.097 --> 00:16:08.044
Wait for my friends to arrive.

153
00:17:51.248 --> 00:17:55.247
Okay, get this bastard off my car!

154
00:18:03.588 --> 00:18:04.828
Faster!

155
00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:19.189
Damn, this kid is determined.

156
00:18:28.603 --> 00:18:30.675
Do you have anything stronger?

157
00:18:36.872 --> 00:18:38.923
I like it.

158
00:18:42.089 --> 00:18:43.297
Keep it steady.

159
00:18:49.629 --> 00:18:51.566
I got him!

160
00:18:51.608 --> 00:18:53.659
What the fuck!

161
00:19:17.497 --> 00:19:18.705
Shit!

162
00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:47.759
Get out of the car!
Get out of the car now!

163
00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:50.853
That's George the Greek.
Check your most wanted list.

164
00:19:50.895 --> 00:19:52.061
Get out of the car right now!

165
00:19:52.072 --> 00:19:56.060
I'm Detective Collier,
undercover narcotics.

166
00:19:56.071 --> 00:19:58.320
- Show us your ID.
- Sure.

167
00:20:38.914 --> 00:20:40.851
You're next.

168
00:20:54.483 --> 00:20:56.524
ID please.

169
00:20:56.525 --> 00:20:58.712
All right, I take over.

170
00:21:00.669 --> 00:21:03.752
- How long do you need?
- One hour tops.

171
00:21:25.684 --> 00:21:28.871
- Here you go Sam.
- Thank you Lola.

172
00:21:32.005 --> 00:21:35.098
- Can I help you?
- Lola.

173
00:22:04.393 --> 00:22:07.413
Grandpa, what was our deal?

174
00:22:08.528 --> 00:22:12.484
- One a day.
- What's all that down on the ground?

175
00:22:12.485 --> 00:22:15.713
Come on, how many
pleasures I got left, huh?

176
00:22:16.692 --> 00:22:18.838
I can't even enjoy reading my paper.

177
00:22:18.848 --> 00:22:20.795
Explain this to me.

178
00:22:20.827 --> 00:22:23.013
He's a bad guy and we took him down.

179
00:22:23.014 --> 00:22:25.970
Most of what you're reading here
is blown out of proportion.

180
00:22:25.971 --> 00:22:28.189
You can't believe everything
that you read.

181
00:22:28.231 --> 00:22:30.137
Like where it says, uh...

182
00:22:30.179 --> 00:22:34.551
"The unidentified undercover
hanging on at 80 miles an hour."

183
00:22:34.552 --> 00:22:35.583
Exaggeration

184
00:22:35.636 --> 00:22:38.541
"Over 300 rounds fired."

185
00:22:38.552 --> 00:22:40.624
Looks like a 100 rounds, maybe.

186
00:22:40.666 --> 00:22:45.779
I am so close to taking down Tremaine.

187
00:22:45.810 --> 00:22:47.955
So close to making him pay.

188
00:22:48.007 --> 00:22:52.236
Revenge and justice
are not the same thing.

189
00:22:54.287 --> 00:22:57.474
And your grandmother is gone.

190
00:22:57.526 --> 00:23:00.327
Your father is gone.

191
00:23:00.338 --> 00:23:02.452
You are all I got left.

192
00:23:02.493 --> 00:23:04.711
And I'm gonna be around
for a very long time

193
00:23:04.712 --> 00:23:07.741
because I'm a very
healthy old man, okay?

194
00:23:07.742 --> 00:23:08.804
All right, so here's the deal.

195
00:23:08.857 --> 00:23:11.835
- I'll get this one last scumbag.
- Okay.

196
00:23:12.918 --> 00:23:15.136
And you keep this to one a day.

197
00:23:16.251 --> 00:23:19.166
I'll cut this out altogether right now

198
00:23:19.208 --> 00:23:22.468
and you forget about going
after that last scumbag.

199
00:23:25.457 --> 00:23:26.560
Yeah.

200
00:23:28.654 --> 00:23:30.737
Just like I thought.

201
00:23:44.192 --> 00:23:46.243
Move, bitch.

202
00:23:52.564 --> 00:23:54.710
Whatchu looking at, fool?

203
00:23:58.823 --> 00:24:00.896
Got your ass.

204
00:24:23.838 --> 00:24:25.817
You Latino?
Where are you from?

205
00:24:25.921 --> 00:24:27.827
Mexico?

206
00:24:28.847 --> 00:24:30.086
Brazil?

207
00:24:37.387 --> 00:24:40.344
What's going on here Rayzah?

208
00:24:43.437 --> 00:24:44.614
Nothing.

209
00:24:44.760 --> 00:24:47.634
Me and home girl gonna chill later.

210
00:25:14.992 --> 00:25:17.793
Let me get down to business.

211
00:25:17.981 --> 00:25:20.116
Lola, please.

212
00:25:24.229 --> 00:25:26.302
- What do you want?
- Your boyfriend.

213
00:25:26.312 --> 00:25:28.187
I don't have a boyfriend.

214
00:25:28.228 --> 00:25:29.540
You and Lino broke up?

215
00:25:29.551 --> 00:25:32.394
I haven't see him in years.

216
00:25:32.498 --> 00:25:34.570
That's not what I heard.

217
00:25:34.623 --> 00:25:38.715
Really? Well, I guess you'll just
have to add me to the list then.

218
00:25:38.726 --> 00:25:39.819
What list is that?

219
00:25:39.830 --> 00:25:42.891
The list of people who don't
give a shit about what you heard.

220
00:25:43.964 --> 00:25:45.141
That's cute.

221
00:25:46.016 --> 00:25:48.202
You listen to this.

222
00:25:49.109 --> 00:25:50.244
I suggest we get along.

223
00:25:50.296 --> 00:25:54.356
Because your pretty ass ain't going
nowhere until Lino shows up.

224
00:25:58.669 --> 00:26:01.657
- Hey Lola.
- Lino, what the hell are you doing?

225
00:26:01.658 --> 00:26:04.678
- If you're going to be mad, I can go.
- Your full of bullshit, I know it!

226
00:26:04.709 --> 00:26:05.813
Can you two work out your relationship

227
00:26:05.823 --> 00:26:07.802
when you don't got a gun to my throat?

228
00:26:07.875 --> 00:26:11.166
His having a gun to your throat
is the issue in our relationship.

229
00:26:11.176 --> 00:26:14.092
All right, everybody just cool down.

230
00:26:14.134 --> 00:26:15.196
Should I take the shot?

231
00:26:15.206 --> 00:26:17.424
Nigga's got a 45 against my neck!

232
00:26:17.466 --> 00:26:19.372
Move!

233
00:26:20.320 --> 00:26:22.361
You too!

234
00:26:27.714 --> 00:26:29.901
Tell Tyrel Glenn to step off.

235
00:26:29.942 --> 00:26:32.816
Get back! Back!

236
00:26:32.827 --> 00:26:35.076
Let's negotiate.
We don't need a blood spill man.

237
00:26:35.087 --> 00:26:38.201
Stop selling dope in the neighborhood,
end of negotiation.

238
00:26:40.158 --> 00:26:43.210
Let the mad man through.
How about this.

239
00:26:43.356 --> 00:26:45.293
I forget about the 20 keys.

240
00:26:45.303 --> 00:26:47.407
You go back with your
pretty girl in one piece.

241
00:26:47.448 --> 00:26:50.541
- And we stay of each other business.
- Not good enough.

242
00:26:50.791 --> 00:26:53.810
How far are you gonna walk out before one of
these niggas puts a shot in your back, huh?

243
00:26:53.811 --> 00:26:55.863
- You get it?
- Back!

244
00:26:55.936 --> 00:26:58.914
Maybe I get hit.
Maybe we all die.

245
00:26:58.956 --> 00:27:02.007
- Maybe your pretty girl get hit, huh?
- Back off.

246
00:27:05.215 --> 00:27:08.360
My boys, they are going to kill you!

247
00:27:08.401 --> 00:27:12.525
You think you can go back
and pretend nothing happened?

248
00:27:12.577 --> 00:27:14.451
And for what, huh?

249
00:27:14.452 --> 00:27:15.733
They will get in here, Lino.

250
00:27:15.775 --> 00:27:18.576
I'm not so sure about that.

251
00:27:18.899 --> 00:27:22.752
- Come on you son of a bitch.
- Move!

252
00:27:24.876 --> 00:27:28.032
- How is it?
- He's locked the door from the outside.

253
00:27:28.074 --> 00:27:30.219
Useless, all of you!

254
00:27:41.560 --> 00:27:42.653
Open the door!

255
00:27:44.684 --> 00:27:47.735
Tyrel Glenn little sister
is about to wake up.

256
00:28:03.586 --> 00:28:06.533
That's my Mustang you know.
That's my baby.

257
00:28:06.543 --> 00:28:09.657
- The keys.
- Son of a bitch.

258
00:28:09.772 --> 00:28:12.833
- Get back!
- You drive.

259
00:28:15.020 --> 00:28:17.936
Don't wreck my car woman.
You're gonna regret it.

260
00:28:17.968 --> 00:28:19.071
- Shut up!
- In the back!

261
00:28:19.123 --> 00:28:21.196
Man, I'm 6'3,
I can't fit back there.

262
00:28:21.238 --> 00:28:24.351
You're about to get
a couple of inches shorter.

263
00:28:41.014 --> 00:28:43.222
We're going to get these bitches!

264
00:29:19.442 --> 00:29:21.660
Shoot the tire! Shoot!

265
00:29:28.929 --> 00:29:31.074
Watch out, woman!

266
00:29:31.085 --> 00:29:33.064
You know how much I spent on this car?

267
00:29:33.095 --> 00:29:36.052
I'll take care of it, I promise.

268
00:29:56.068 --> 00:29:59.161
You don't need me here.
Just let me out, you can keep the damn car.

269
00:29:59.192 --> 00:30:02.077
Always negotiating, huh?

270
00:30:29.216 --> 00:30:31.268
Stay right there!

271
00:30:34.569 --> 00:30:36.714
- Open that door!
- Drop it! Drop the weapon!

272
00:30:36.725 --> 00:30:40.713
- Don't shoot!
- Get out of the car!

273
00:30:40.755 --> 00:30:41.921
We're here to see your captain,
don't shoot.

274
00:30:41.949 --> 00:30:42.949
Get down!

275
00:30:42.973 --> 00:30:45.889
Stay cool.

276
00:30:50.242 --> 00:30:51.346
Move!

277
00:30:56.283 --> 00:30:59.407
This is Tremaine Alexander.
I'm sure you know him.

278
00:30:59.448 --> 00:31:00.625
Yes, we know.

279
00:31:01.500 --> 00:31:03.552
Put your gun down, son.

280
00:31:03.760 --> 00:31:05.811
Nobody move.

281
00:31:07.790 --> 00:31:09.935
Everybody stay cool.

282
00:31:15.226 --> 00:31:18.246
Put your gun down, son.
Give me your weapon.

283
00:31:19.183 --> 00:31:20.391
You did good.

284
00:31:20.402 --> 00:31:21.464
Lock him up!

285
00:31:21.516 --> 00:31:24.536
What? Wait! What
the hell are you doing?

286
00:31:24.567 --> 00:31:27.556
Get your hands off me!
Let me out of here!

287
00:31:27.629 --> 00:31:29.608
Hey! Hey!

288
00:31:29.649 --> 00:31:31.826
Son of bitches!
Let me out!

289
00:31:31.836 --> 00:31:34.783
Hey Mike, how's that new house you got?

290
00:31:34.825 --> 00:31:36.064
Never mind.
Get out of here, Tremaine.

291
00:31:36.075 --> 00:31:39.022
Guess my donation
is coming in handy, huh?

292
00:31:40.001 --> 00:31:42.146
- Come on, Miss Lola.
- I'm not going anywhere with you!

293
00:31:42.157 --> 00:31:45.270
Tremaine!
You son of a bitch! I'll kill you!

294
00:31:45.281 --> 00:31:46.385
Let me go!

295
00:31:46.426 --> 00:31:50.384
It's all politics, Lino.
I'm a politician.

296
00:31:50.530 --> 00:31:52.602
C'est la vie

297
00:31:52.644 --> 00:31:54.694
No! Open the door!

298
00:31:54.695 --> 00:31:57.715
Open this door now!

299
00:32:02.027 --> 00:32:04.172
- You can go.
- Yes, sir!

300
00:32:07.275 --> 00:32:11.379
You gave her to those animals,
you dirty piece of shit.

301
00:32:11.410 --> 00:32:14.430
Sorry son, the way of the world.

302
00:32:36.289 --> 00:32:39.622
Detective Collier,
the Mayor is ready to see you.

303
00:32:43.766 --> 00:32:46.672
Detective, come in.

304
00:32:46.818 --> 00:32:49.004
Detective Collier.
Tom Berringer.

305
00:32:49.005 --> 00:32:51.848
- I was in the force with your dad.
- Nice to meet you.

306
00:32:51.889 --> 00:32:55.045
Your family has a history with the city.

307
00:32:55.055 --> 00:32:58.315
Damien's father led the last
police raid in Brick Mansions.

308
00:32:59.190 --> 00:33:02.449
His unfortunate death pushed
legislation for us to erect the border.

309
00:33:02.460 --> 00:33:05.573
He's a hero, and from what
I hear, you're a lot like him.

310
00:33:05.615 --> 00:33:06.646
Thank you.

311
00:33:06.667 --> 00:33:08.739
We've been made to understand that
you have somewhat of an expertise

312
00:33:08.781 --> 00:33:10.583
in terms of that neighborhood.

313
00:33:10.624 --> 00:33:12.728
Yeah, I know it pretty well.

314
00:33:12.738 --> 00:33:14.852
- Major Reno, U.S. Army.
- Pleasure.

315
00:33:14.894 --> 00:33:18.154
Detective, this is a situation that
demands the best of the best.

316
00:33:18.164 --> 00:33:22.090
Last night a government transport

317
00:33:22.121 --> 00:33:26.225
travelling at a time and route with
minimal civilian traffic was hijacked.

318
00:33:43.179 --> 00:33:45.199
What are they transporting?

319
00:33:52.458 --> 00:33:56.488
N.A.D, Neutron Assisted Device.
A neutron bomb.

320
00:33:56.530 --> 00:33:57.737
We prefer the word device.

321
00:33:57.738 --> 00:33:59.789
Bomb has such negative connonations.

322
00:33:59.831 --> 00:34:02.736
The device was fitted with
an anti theft mechanism.

323
00:34:02.747 --> 00:34:07.048
Which is triggered if the case
should be open the wrong way.

324
00:34:08.162 --> 00:34:10.141
Device activated.

325
00:34:10.151 --> 00:34:12.161
What the fuck?

326
00:34:12.192 --> 00:34:15.180
We need you to infiltrate,
locate the device,

327
00:34:15.181 --> 00:34:17.295
and contact us for the code to disarm it.

328
00:34:17.337 --> 00:34:18.441
Nah, that can't be done.

329
00:34:18.451 --> 00:34:19.586
That'd take time, planning.

330
00:34:19.638 --> 00:34:21.616
We don't know where it's at,
we don't know who has it.

331
00:34:21.617 --> 00:34:23.626
We know where. Brick Mansions.

332
00:34:23.627 --> 00:34:25.606
We know who.

333
00:34:26.897 --> 00:34:28.875
That's Tremaine Alexander.

334
00:34:28.876 --> 00:34:31.865
Ex-soldier turned illegal arms dealer.

335
00:34:31.896 --> 00:34:34.010
He uses military grade weapons,
united the gangs,

336
00:34:34.020 --> 00:34:36.124
and tookover the city's drug trade.

337
00:34:36.176 --> 00:34:38.228
Rules with an iron fist.

338
00:34:38.259 --> 00:34:40.404
I spent my entire career
trying to take down Tremaine.

339
00:34:40.415 --> 00:34:43.435
But he never leaves Brick Mansions
and there's checkpoints everywhere.

340
00:34:43.466 --> 00:34:45.549
- You know the routes around.
- Yeah, but then what?

341
00:34:45.590 --> 00:34:47.663
We have no intel inside.
No eyes.

342
00:34:47.673 --> 00:34:48.746
We have your eyes.

343
00:34:48.788 --> 00:34:51.808
Lino Dupree, French Carribean expat.

344
00:34:51.849 --> 00:34:53.994
Spent most of his adult live
in Brick Mansions.

345
00:34:53.995 --> 00:34:55.941
Knows it like the back of his hands.

346
00:34:55.942 --> 00:34:58.962
So the best idea you can come up with
is to send me into this shit

347
00:34:59.004 --> 00:35:00.108
with a convict as my partner?

348
00:35:00.118 --> 00:35:01.180
Yeah.

349
00:35:02.097 --> 00:35:04.106
And you got 10 hours, Detective.

350
00:35:04.107 --> 00:35:06.189
What's he locked up for anyway?

351
00:35:09.324 --> 00:35:10.501
Killed a cop.

352
00:35:24.018 --> 00:35:26.164
Dupree, let's go.

353
00:35:57.343 --> 00:35:59.489
Get in the van!

354
00:35:59.499 --> 00:36:01.405
Get in!

355
00:36:53.496 --> 00:36:54.777
I'll be back.

356
00:37:42.630 --> 00:37:45.650
- Thanks.
- Yeah, have a good day.

357
00:37:49.753 --> 00:37:53.054
Hey, hey, wait!
I need this van!

358
00:37:54.096 --> 00:37:57.053
Are you kidding me?
Who do you think you are man?

359
00:37:59.282 --> 00:38:02.188
You trying to hijack me?

360
00:38:09.530 --> 00:38:10.810
It's my van!

361
00:38:13.695 --> 00:38:15.715
I don't think so.

362
00:38:15.893 --> 00:38:17.934
This is my van.

363
00:38:21.027 --> 00:38:22.235
Really?

364
00:38:32.461 --> 00:38:35.721
It's my van, but if you want a lift
hurry up, the bus is leaving.

365
00:38:46.052 --> 00:38:48.102
Recalculating itinerary.

366
00:38:48.103 --> 00:38:50.207
- Where are we headed?
- Brick Mansions.

367
00:38:50.217 --> 00:38:52.331
There's no way you can drive
this van past the barricades.

368
00:38:52.373 --> 00:38:56.362
Three minutes ago we were
handcuffed in the back of this thing.

369
00:38:57.518 --> 00:38:59.694
Why is a guy like you
going to Brick Mansions?

370
00:38:59.705 --> 00:39:02.579
I'm after Tremaine Alexander.
He killed a friend of mine.

371
00:39:02.589 --> 00:39:04.662
Same asshole kidnapped my girlfriend.

372
00:39:04.714 --> 00:39:05.922
Ex girlfriend.

373
00:39:05.963 --> 00:39:07.942
Sound like we got something in common.

374
00:39:07.973 --> 00:39:10.962
- How do you plan to get inside?
- There's an old smuggling route.

375
00:39:10.993 --> 00:39:13.076
Take a right at 50 metres.

376
00:39:18.262 --> 00:39:20.481
- Better buckle up.
- I prefer to be free.

377
00:39:20.522 --> 00:39:22.501
Suit yourself.

378
00:39:28.687 --> 00:39:30.864
We can't lose them at East port.

379
00:39:44.464 --> 00:39:46.506
That's a checkpoint.

380
00:39:48.453 --> 00:39:50.536
This GPS is broken!

381
00:39:50.577 --> 00:39:52.629
Wrong direction.
Please make a U-turn now.

382
00:39:52.660 --> 00:39:54.681
Shit!

383
00:39:54.743 --> 00:39:55.951
Stop your vehicle now!

384
00:39:55.993 --> 00:39:58.805
I repeat, stop your vehicle now!

385
00:39:58.846 --> 00:40:00.919
What are you doing?
Are you crazy?

386
00:40:00.971 --> 00:40:03.043
You need to trust me man.

387
00:40:11.395 --> 00:40:13.436
Shit.

388
00:40:13.686 --> 00:40:15.623
I can't see shit.

389
00:40:16.675 --> 00:40:17.810
Shit.

390
00:40:28.141 --> 00:40:30.120
Steerings gone.

391
00:40:30.297 --> 00:40:32.369
Brakes are gone.

392
00:40:33.452 --> 00:40:35.400
Work on it!

393
00:40:46.907 --> 00:40:50.969
Shit.
Old smuggling route, huh?

394
00:40:51.177 --> 00:40:53.010
Yeah.

395
00:41:00.352 --> 00:41:02.424
You got to get the hell out of here man.

396
00:41:05.559 --> 00:41:07.609
- Not we.
- What the hell are you doing?

397
00:41:07.610 --> 00:41:09.829
- You're a cop.
- Are you crazy?

398
00:41:09.912 --> 00:41:13.026
Come on.
I can smell a cop a mile away.

399
00:41:13.869 --> 00:41:15.046
Hey come on, you can't leave me like this.

400
00:41:15.088 --> 00:41:17.160
Come on, help me get out of here.
What am I suppose to do?

401
00:41:17.171 --> 00:41:21.097
Look in the police manual under
"shit happens."

402
00:41:21.128 --> 00:41:22.409
Yeah, that's really funny.

403
00:41:24.398 --> 00:41:27.387
French asshole.

404
00:41:34.645 --> 00:41:35.958
Shit, this is your car, huh?

405
00:41:35.968 --> 00:41:39.821
- Hell yeah.
- The brake's failed.

406
00:41:39.863 --> 00:41:41.583
You get me out of here,
we'll sort this out.

407
00:41:42.987 --> 00:41:45.237
You are dead.

408
00:42:39.275 --> 00:42:40.275
Shit.

409
00:42:48.763 --> 00:42:50.814
Be careful.

410
00:42:50.887 --> 00:42:52.761
You're dead, look at you.

411
00:42:52.762 --> 00:42:55.011
Yo, put that down. Tremaine.
Put that down.

412
00:43:04.332 --> 00:43:06.404
Que pasa mamacita?

413
00:43:06.456 --> 00:43:08.601
Hope you've been enjoying
our accomodations.

414
00:43:08.612 --> 00:43:11.486
I'm so done with this place.

415
00:43:11.528 --> 00:43:15.860
Look, you keep it cool with me,
I keep it cool with you.

416
00:43:17.776 --> 00:43:20.963
I try to press education in my boys,
but they are a different breed.

417
00:43:20.973 --> 00:43:23.025
If they're not out shooting niggas
in the streets

418
00:43:23.067 --> 00:43:26.159
they shooting them on video screens.

419
00:43:26.160 --> 00:43:27.326
So I give them a job, you know.

420
00:43:27.336 --> 00:43:29.315
These niggas feed their families.

421
00:43:29.357 --> 00:43:33.543
Look, between me and you,
I like Lino.

422
00:43:33.554 --> 00:43:36.614
He has a cause,
even it gets him killed.

423
00:43:36.615 --> 00:43:39.771
People like you remind me
why everyone hates us.

424
00:43:40.885 --> 00:43:43.978
You and him are lot alike.

425
00:43:44.020 --> 00:43:47.165
- I can see why you together.
- Separated.

426
00:43:47.217 --> 00:43:51.310
Don't worry, mamacita.
You will hear about him soon.

427
00:43:52.184 --> 00:43:53.424
Oh, you haven't heard the good news?

428
00:43:53.434 --> 00:43:55.443
Lino escaped.

429
00:43:55.444 --> 00:43:57.495
Not sure if he's gonna come in here.

430
00:43:57.537 --> 00:44:00.630
And I wouldn't wanna be
old when he gets here.

431
00:44:00.661 --> 00:44:04.692
Tremaine, we all good on the roof.
Do you wanna head back?

432
00:44:06.920 --> 00:44:09.795
Rayzah here will keep you company.

433
00:44:13.065 --> 00:44:15.085
Yo, get your hands of my chips.

434
00:44:16.158 --> 00:44:18.167
Oh, shit.

435
00:44:18.209 --> 00:44:19.313
Move!

436
00:44:39.235 --> 00:44:43.224
- How did you know I was a cop?
- You don't belong here.

437
00:44:44.307 --> 00:44:47.327
- How did you find me?
- I put a bug in your pocket.

438
00:44:53.544 --> 00:44:57.668
Cop's tricks.
That's all you people have.

439
00:44:57.720 --> 00:44:59.865
No, we have the law.
It just something you don't care about.

440
00:44:59.907 --> 00:45:01.885
The law means nothing without justice.

441
00:45:01.886 --> 00:45:03.937
That's pretty high for somebody
who killed a cop.

442
00:45:03.969 --> 00:45:07.093
That cop was a corrupt piece of shit,
no better than Tremaine.

443
00:45:07.207 --> 00:45:09.280
I'm gonna find Tremaine.

444
00:45:09.290 --> 00:45:11.341
I'm gonna find him before
the weapon he hijacked

445
00:45:11.342 --> 00:45:13.445
kills everybody inside
the Brick Mansions.

446
00:45:14.539 --> 00:45:16.549
Probably didn't occur to you there's
somebody on the outside

447
00:45:16.591 --> 00:45:19.151
that actually gives a shit about
what happen in here now did you?

448
00:45:21.693 --> 00:45:23.943
Not everybody out there is an asshole.

449
00:45:23.953 --> 00:45:28.077
Just like not everybody in here
is a junkie or a thief.

450
00:45:29.129 --> 00:45:31.077
You enjoy yourself.

451
00:45:31.108 --> 00:45:33.357
And if I find your girlfriend
I'll tell her you said hi.

452
00:45:33.399 --> 00:45:36.387
They will shoot you and
take your badge as trophy.

453
00:45:36.388 --> 00:45:38.366
At least I'll die trying.

454
00:45:38.377 --> 00:45:42.532
Which is a hell lot better than sitting
around bitching about how the world sucks.

455
00:45:43.615 --> 00:45:48.968
If you're not bullshitting about that bomb,
maybe I can save Lola before we all go down.

456
00:45:49.770 --> 00:45:51.842
And the first chance you get,
what are you gonna do?

457
00:45:51.894 --> 00:45:53.934
You gonna put a bullet
in the back of my head?

458
00:45:53.935 --> 00:45:56.227
I could've kill you already.

459
00:46:09.859 --> 00:46:11.837
So what's your plan?

460
00:46:11.941 --> 00:46:14.889
- You got a phone?
- Yeah.

461
00:46:25.355 --> 00:46:28.500
Tremaine, it's Lino.
I'm coming over.

462
00:46:29.593 --> 00:46:32.612
So that's it?
You just throwing him a line?

463
00:46:32.613 --> 00:46:34.727
A line he'll never expect.

464
00:46:36.789 --> 00:46:38.966
This is gonna be a lot of fun.

465
00:46:41.892 --> 00:46:43.902
Not bad, right?

466
00:46:59.825 --> 00:47:02.804
Hello, Lola.

467
00:47:05.866 --> 00:47:07.115
Fuck!

468
00:47:40.305 --> 00:47:43.419
Where are you going?

469
00:47:45.408 --> 00:47:48.595
I knew you'd be fun to play with
the second I saw you.

470
00:48:10.641 --> 00:48:13.661
I really love this game.

471
00:48:32.292 --> 00:48:34.437
Do I look like a bitch?

472
00:48:37.676 --> 00:48:40.664
Hey, Rayzah.
I heard shouts.

473
00:48:40.665 --> 00:48:43.716
You can play but not too hard, okay?

474
00:48:44.799 --> 00:48:45.935
You are one lucky bitch.

475
00:48:57.442 --> 00:48:59.390
What do we got here?

476
00:48:59.431 --> 00:49:01.441
Take us to Tremaine.

477
00:49:12.105 --> 00:49:16.177
K2, get your fat ass up here!
We got a guest coming!

478
00:49:18.260 --> 00:49:21.207
Yeti, move it!
Upstairs, now!

479
00:49:21.217 --> 00:49:23.259
It's show time!

480
00:49:27.508 --> 00:49:29.715
Damien, you see that?

481
00:49:43.275 --> 00:49:45.357
Lino.

482
00:49:46.409 --> 00:49:49.325
Surprised that your back here so soon.

483
00:49:49.356 --> 00:49:52.418
You see?
He is surprised.

484
00:49:52.658 --> 00:49:55.678
- Who's your boy?
- I'm his driver.

485
00:49:55.719 --> 00:49:57.656
He's a cop.

486
00:49:58.812 --> 00:50:02.874
- Comes for his bomb.
- Thanks. Thanks for that.

487
00:50:02.916 --> 00:50:06.238
- That's great.
- Wow, a cop.

488
00:50:06.248 --> 00:50:09.091
Haven't seen one of those
around here in years.

489
00:50:09.101 --> 00:50:13.288
I believe the police station closed around
the same time as the school, the hospital.

490
00:50:13.340 --> 00:50:16.454
The government thought
we didn't need that around here.

491
00:50:16.537 --> 00:50:19.484
So, what, you're the new Sheriff in town?

492
00:50:19.526 --> 00:50:21.598
You're a brave man.

493
00:50:23.827 --> 00:50:25.806
Where's Lola?

494
00:50:25.816 --> 00:50:26.910
We'll get to her.

495
00:50:26.920 --> 00:50:29.107
Let's talk about this bomb.
You're here to buy?

496
00:50:30.086 --> 00:50:31.992
I came to disarm it.

497
00:50:32.033 --> 00:50:34.137
This is gonna make you a little
bit anxious. It's ticking.

498
00:50:34.147 --> 00:50:37.272
Tremaine Alexander don't do anxious.
I cause anxious.

499
00:50:37.313 --> 00:50:40.427
I could be halfway down South
before this thing goes off

500
00:50:40.479 --> 00:50:42.457
or you can make me an offer.

501
00:50:42.458 --> 00:50:44.738
I'll offer you to disable it before
it blows us all up, you like that?

502
00:50:44.780 --> 00:50:48.851
That won't fly. How about I just
send it back the way I found it?

503
00:50:48.852 --> 00:50:50.924
K2, let the sunshine in.

504
00:50:50.966 --> 00:50:53.986
Gentleman, please,
your gonna love the view.

505
00:51:13.867 --> 00:51:15.887
Only a crazy person would have a rocket.

506
00:51:15.918 --> 00:51:17.991
We live in a war,
so we prepared for war.

507
00:51:18.001 --> 00:51:22.104
I can destroy downtown
at a push of this button.

508
00:51:22.135 --> 00:51:24.114
Let's talk numbers.

509
00:51:24.156 --> 00:51:27.249
You let all those people die for money?
That's low even for you.

510
00:51:27.280 --> 00:51:30.467
Nigga, where I come from,
everything is about cash.

511
00:51:30.508 --> 00:51:32.560
You know what that means, right?

512
00:51:33.643 --> 00:51:36.590
First I need to know Lola's okay.

513
00:51:40.829 --> 00:51:42.037
Rayzah.

514
00:51:42.880 --> 00:51:44.932
Look at number three.

515
00:51:56.544 --> 00:51:58.554
What do you see?

516
00:52:04.979 --> 00:52:07.822
What do you see Lino?

517
00:52:12.279 --> 00:52:15.195
No, no, wait.

518
00:52:15.237 --> 00:52:17.215
Coward!

519
00:52:17.216 --> 00:52:19.434
- You wanna die here man?
- Don't shoot.

520
00:52:23.610 --> 00:52:27.703
Now's not the time.
Lino, not now.

521
00:52:27.817 --> 00:52:29.857
Now you boys all excited

522
00:52:29.858 --> 00:52:32.920
let's do this shit the uptown way.

523
00:52:32.951 --> 00:52:35.138
I got a rocket, I got a bomb
and I got a pretty woman.

524
00:52:35.180 --> 00:52:38.127
I say we starts the bidding at
10 million dollars.

525
00:52:38.138 --> 00:52:40.075
- Do I hear 11?
- 11.

526
00:52:40.116 --> 00:52:41.324
- 11 million.
- 12

527
00:52:41.335 --> 00:52:44.240
Oh, that's a spicy bid right there.
We gettin there now.

528
00:52:44.282 --> 00:52:47.437
- 15.
- 15? Stop the bullshit!

529
00:52:47.448 --> 00:52:50.666
You tell me how much it's worth to you?
How much the people downtown worth?

530
00:52:50.707 --> 00:52:53.737
Because around here,
people lives aren't worth a shit.

531
00:52:53.738 --> 00:52:56.852
Look around, Sheriff,
this used to be a palace.

532
00:52:56.893 --> 00:52:58.966
Doorman, woman waiting on table.

533
00:52:58.987 --> 00:53:02.069
Where the bitches at now?
In the alley, shooting up.

534
00:53:02.111 --> 00:53:04.161
Because of drugs dealer like you.

535
00:53:04.162 --> 00:53:06.172
I didn't cause this reality.

536
00:53:06.214 --> 00:53:09.401
I just help them ease the pain.

537
00:53:09.411 --> 00:53:10.505
Let's get back to that money.

538
00:53:10.557 --> 00:53:12.598
- We're at 15 million, right?
- 15.

539
00:53:12.639 --> 00:53:13.670
- Do I hear 20 million?
- 20.

540
00:53:13.681 --> 00:53:16.555
Okay, stop the game.
What's it gonna take?

541
00:53:16.597 --> 00:53:18.616
You got 3 million people downtown.

542
00:53:18.617 --> 00:53:20.867
10 dollars per person.
Price of a happy meal.

543
00:53:20.877 --> 00:53:22.814
That's 30 million dollars for me.

544
00:53:22.856 --> 00:53:24.928
- Then 30 million?
- 30 million.

545
00:53:24.970 --> 00:53:27.020
Done.
30 million it is.

546
00:53:27.021 --> 00:53:28.271
30 million.

547
00:53:28.313 --> 00:53:33.311
Sold to Lino Dupree and the
new Sheriff of Brick Mansions.

548
00:53:33.416 --> 00:53:35.394
Call your people and make it happen.

549
00:53:36.550 --> 00:53:39.633
And Lino, stay out of my business.

550
00:53:45.756 --> 00:53:47.036
- Yes?
- It's Detective Collier.

551
00:53:47.037 --> 00:53:50.994
- Collier? Where are we now?
- We're close. Really close.

552
00:53:51.005 --> 00:53:54.223
- Close enough to punch the code in?
- No, unfortunately no.

553
00:53:54.233 --> 00:53:55.296
What's the problem?

554
00:53:55.306 --> 00:53:57.420
The problem is that
the new owner wants to sell.

555
00:53:57.430 --> 00:53:59.409
Are you sure the bomb is there?

556
00:53:59.440 --> 00:54:03.398
Yes, and I can tell you that there's
only 48 minutes before it blows up.

557
00:54:03.408 --> 00:54:04.512
Okay.

558
00:54:04.689 --> 00:54:07.677
- How do we proceed?
- You have an Hawaiian bank account?

559
00:54:07.678 --> 00:54:10.865
- I want it in cash, man.
- They can't do cash.

560
00:54:10.948 --> 00:54:13.895
- We still got an account in Hawaii?
- We do.

561
00:54:13.937 --> 00:54:15.145
Give him the numbers.

562
00:54:15.155 --> 00:54:18.061
Bank, 83675.

563
00:54:18.071 --> 00:54:20.144
Bank, 83675.

564
00:54:20.154 --> 00:54:22.206
Account, 0210-84.

565
00:54:22.237 --> 00:54:24.528
Account, 0210-84.

566
00:54:25.476 --> 00:54:28.423
- What's he asking?
- 30 million dollars.

567
00:54:28.673 --> 00:54:29.673
Hold on.

568
00:54:29.714 --> 00:54:32.588
Tremaine wants 30 million
for the device.

569
00:54:32.599 --> 00:54:34.671
The city damn near broke.

570
00:54:35.827 --> 00:54:37.900
- We cannot do that, Detective.
- All right, good.

571
00:54:37.910 --> 00:54:40.055
You have to find another solution.

572
00:54:47.366 --> 00:54:48.459
Exactly.

573
00:54:49.345 --> 00:54:51.395
All right, good, yeah.

574
00:54:51.396 --> 00:54:52.531
Perfect.

575
00:54:52.646 --> 00:54:55.666
That's a wrap.
They're sending in the money.

576
00:54:55.697 --> 00:54:58.654
- Let's go disable that bomb.
- Hold on.

577
00:54:58.655 --> 00:55:01.748
Wait a minute,
let my man verify the transfer.

578
00:55:01.987 --> 00:55:04.944
Bank doesn't open for another 25 minutes.

579
00:55:04.945 --> 00:55:06.080
25 minutes.

580
00:55:06.122 --> 00:55:08.267
Well, that's enough time for me
to finish dinner.

581
00:55:08.277 --> 00:55:10.224
K2.

582
00:55:10.225 --> 00:55:13.214
Show our guests to the presidential suite.

583
00:55:14.224 --> 00:55:16.442
Nice doing business with you, Sheriff.

584
00:55:16.484 --> 00:55:17.379
Move!

585
00:55:17.390 --> 00:55:19.639
Sometimes you dont gotta
be a rocket scientist.

586
00:55:19.681 --> 00:55:21.732
Just got to have a rocket.

587
00:55:46.674 --> 00:55:47.819
Move!

588
00:55:47.820 --> 00:55:49.798
Face the rack!

589
00:55:50.673 --> 00:55:51.808
- On your knees!
- Shit.

590
00:55:51.850 --> 00:55:53.933
Put your damn hands behind your head!

591
00:55:53.943 --> 00:55:56.995
I got to tell you,
I'm claustrophobic.

592
00:55:58.182 --> 00:56:02.097
Until Tremaine gets his 30 million,
their lives worth more than both of us.

593
00:56:02.139 --> 00:56:05.232
They die, you die.

594
00:56:11.595 --> 00:56:13.573
So you're not having a plan gets us in.

595
00:56:13.574 --> 00:56:15.854
Hey, you know where the bomb is,
I know where Lola is.

596
00:56:15.896 --> 00:56:17.947
And in 25 minutes, we act.

597
00:56:17.948 --> 00:56:20.020
In 25 minutes Tremaine is gonna shoot us.

598
00:56:20.072 --> 00:56:22.176
The device is gonna kill 3 million people.

599
00:56:22.186 --> 00:56:25.278
What? When he gets his money,
everybody walks away.

600
00:56:25.279 --> 00:56:26.383
There is no money.

601
00:56:26.394 --> 00:56:29.277
The city can't pay.
I was just trying to buy us some time.

602
00:56:29.278 --> 00:56:30.413
Forget what I said before.

603
00:56:30.465 --> 00:56:33.444
Don't trust your instinct.
They're shit.

604
00:56:33.652 --> 00:56:35.703
I should've killed Tremaine
when I had the chance.

605
00:56:35.704 --> 00:56:37.724
Shut up.

606
00:56:39.776 --> 00:56:40.880
Wait.

607
00:56:40.890 --> 00:56:44.077
That story about Tremaine killing
your friend, it's true?

608
00:56:44.879 --> 00:56:48.179
That's my father. He used to
lead some officers on a drug raid.

609
00:56:48.180 --> 00:56:52.345
He got separated from his squad. Tremaine's
boys captured him and killed him.

610
00:56:52.387 --> 00:56:54.262
I'm sorry.

611
00:56:55.376 --> 00:56:58.469
Let's go make him pay.
Back me up.

612
00:57:02.676 --> 00:57:04.717
Help him man!

613
00:57:05.936 --> 00:57:08.924
Stop it!

614
00:57:08.925 --> 00:57:11.112
- Son of a bitch.
- What happened?

615
00:57:11.153 --> 00:57:13.017
Oh, shit.

616
00:57:13.028 --> 00:57:14.267
- He's not breathing.
- What?

617
00:57:14.278 --> 00:57:16.225
We got to get him out of here.

618
00:57:16.360 --> 00:57:18.308
Shit.

619
00:57:18.443 --> 00:57:21.328
- Oh, come on!
- He's not breathing, come on!

620
00:57:21.370 --> 00:57:23.577
- Okay, go!
- Open the gate!

621
00:57:23.588 --> 00:57:25.494
I will talk to the boss.

622
00:57:27.555 --> 00:57:28.764
Go!

623
00:57:37.043 --> 00:57:40.125
- Something's not right about this.
- You think they'll come up with the money?

624
00:57:40.136 --> 00:57:41.198
We'll see.

625
00:57:41.208 --> 00:57:42.312
Tell me how you got that bomb again.

626
00:57:42.323 --> 00:57:46.478
Bomb? Yeah. These dudes at base told
me about some weapon being moved.

627
00:57:46.520 --> 00:57:49.580
No security.
Keys left in the truck.

628
00:57:49.581 --> 00:57:51.560
Easy money, baby.

629
00:57:51.602 --> 00:57:54.820
That's whats bothering me man.
You can never trust easy.

630
00:58:00.985 --> 00:58:03.120
- I'm okay.
- You're crazy.

631
00:58:03.172 --> 00:58:06.150
We're out of the room.
Your turn cop.

632
00:58:06.161 --> 00:58:09.420
Is this some kind of game to you?

633
00:58:10.326 --> 00:58:11.503
On three.

634
00:58:12.555 --> 00:58:14.461
Three!

635
00:58:25.968 --> 00:58:28.009
Go, go, go!

636
00:58:28.988 --> 00:58:30.227
This way!

637
00:58:30.311 --> 00:58:32.352
It's them!

638
00:58:33.227 --> 00:58:34.362
Go, go, go!

639
00:58:34.372 --> 00:58:37.392
- You know where we going?
- More or less.

640
00:58:42.714 --> 00:58:43.818
Shit.

641
00:58:47.921 --> 00:58:49.764
Damien!

642
00:58:58.137 --> 00:58:59.418
What the fuck?

643
00:59:03.532 --> 00:59:05.542
Different method, same result.

644
00:59:05.615 --> 00:59:07.520
Let's go.

645
00:59:29.411 --> 00:59:32.535
- It's faster.
- But you still need the key.

646
00:59:32.681 --> 00:59:34.587
Go, go!

647
00:59:34.597 --> 00:59:35.868
I'll drive.

648
00:59:43.001 --> 00:59:45.146
Get out of the way you fool!

649
00:59:47.104 --> 00:59:49.208
Let's get these guys!

650
00:59:53.322 --> 00:59:54.498
Faster!

651
01:00:03.850 --> 01:00:05.995
- Faster!
- You wanna drive?

652
01:00:06.037 --> 01:00:08.110
- Go ahead, drive.
- Whoah, whoah.

653
01:00:11.078 --> 01:00:12.109
I need to get out.

654
01:00:12.150 --> 01:00:14.170
What are you trying to do
Jumping out of the damn car for?

655
01:00:14.171 --> 01:00:15.451
- Where you going?
- I'm trying to get rid of these guys.

656
01:00:15.493 --> 01:00:17.430
Will you shut up?

657
01:00:31.958 --> 01:00:34.103
I don't see them!

658
01:00:39.435 --> 01:00:42.350
- Rooftops back that way!
- Why didn't you tell me that?

659
01:00:42.351 --> 01:00:44.600
- Come on, tell me, which way?
- Left, left!

660
01:00:55.941 --> 01:00:58.118
Lola is in back there!
We don't have much time!

661
01:00:58.160 --> 01:01:00.211
Back where?

662
01:01:08.522 --> 01:01:10.625
Damn.

663
01:01:19.946 --> 01:01:21.820
Come on!

664
01:01:25.268 --> 01:01:28.069
I told you to stay down!

665
01:01:31.245 --> 01:01:34.567
Look, we can't just run to that rooftop.
They're gonna be expecting us.

666
01:01:36.598 --> 01:01:39.648
- You got a better solution?
- I'm working on it.

667
01:01:39.649 --> 01:01:41.701
Can you work while you run?

668
01:01:48.064 --> 01:01:51.209
- Tremaine gonna wild out.
- Come on, this way.

669
01:01:59.634 --> 01:02:02.477
Stay down this time.

670
01:02:09.913 --> 01:02:11.058
They're in the bus!

671
01:02:29.793 --> 01:02:32.668
You two, go check it out.

672
01:03:09.158 --> 01:03:11.210
Let's split up!

673
01:03:43.671 --> 01:03:45.743
- On three!
- Three!

674
01:03:57.292 --> 01:03:59.229
What the...

675
01:04:10.841 --> 01:04:12.851
Shit.

676
01:04:13.903 --> 01:04:16.777
Close enough now?

677
01:04:19.110 --> 01:04:21.162
Thank you.

678
01:04:42.948 --> 01:04:46.041
- Get defense on the line immediately.
- Yes, sir.

679
01:04:51.217 --> 01:04:53.508
Hello. What?

680
01:04:54.382 --> 01:04:56.559
Okay.
I'm gonna bring it up right now.

681
01:04:58.590 --> 01:05:00.631
We have an issue.

682
01:05:00.704 --> 01:05:03.724
These are satellite surveillance
images from Brick Mansions

683
01:05:03.766 --> 01:05:04.901
taken several minutes ago.

684
01:05:04.911 --> 01:05:07.857
- There's the bomb.
- What's that?

685
01:05:07.858 --> 01:05:11.232
That's an old Russian missile.
Has a radius about 5 miles.

686
01:05:11.264 --> 01:05:15.158
- How the hell did they get that?
- Wait, if they launch that...

687
01:05:15.159 --> 01:05:17.304
- The city is ground zero.
- We're gonna have to evacuate.

688
01:05:17.314 --> 01:05:19.324
- No time.
- There's a fallout shelter.

689
01:05:19.335 --> 01:05:21.469
It won't help us against the NAD blast.

690
01:05:21.522 --> 01:05:22.657
What options do we have then?
Drone?

691
01:05:22.667 --> 01:05:26.656
Too late. We'll never get
authorization just like that.

692
01:05:31.904 --> 01:05:34.123
- Bank is open.
- I'll check.

693
01:05:40.319 --> 01:05:43.307
I think they fooled us.
No deposit.

694
01:05:43.308 --> 01:05:45.526
And you wonder why people
don't trust the government.

695
01:05:45.568 --> 01:05:47.619
What the hell is going on?

696
01:05:50.608 --> 01:05:52.618
Not only did they not make the transfer.

697
01:05:53.941 --> 01:05:56.929
They're emptying all of our bank accounts.

698
01:06:00.960 --> 01:06:04.323
Rayzah. We're gonna launch.
Stay clear.

699
01:06:05.334 --> 01:06:07.353
Time's up, bitch.

700
01:06:07.354 --> 01:06:10.374
Downtown is about to get remodeled.

701
01:06:33.452 --> 01:06:36.326
Russian piece of shit.

702
01:06:37.378 --> 01:06:40.471
There goes the controller.
Now I'm gonna get her out of the picture.

703
01:06:45.751 --> 01:06:48.000
Be careful.
You'll hit Lola.

704
01:06:49.125 --> 01:06:51.135
No, I wanna get this one
away from her.

705
01:06:53.186 --> 01:06:57.383
Trem. Trem, they shot the receiver.

706
01:06:58.498 --> 01:07:01.341
Now I got to shoot
the Sheriff and his deputy.

707
01:07:04.652 --> 01:07:07.745
Damn it. Let's go.

708
01:07:08.714 --> 01:07:10.901
For the Brick Mansions!

709
01:07:10.974 --> 01:07:13.817
Time to strap up boys!

710
01:07:13.900 --> 01:07:16.077
We fight or we die!

711
01:07:20.086 --> 01:07:23.231
- What was that?
- Looks like they shot the launch mechanism.

712
01:07:23.314 --> 01:07:26.501
- The missile can't launch.
- We're still in the game.

713
01:07:29.500 --> 01:07:31.646
I want the building sealed down.

714
01:07:46.319 --> 01:07:49.506
Seal the building!
Yeti, with me.

715
01:08:12.209 --> 01:08:13.448
Move it!

716
01:08:26.976 --> 01:08:29.923
That sucks.
Excuse me.

717
01:08:30.027 --> 01:08:33.119
- One, two, three.
- Hey, what are you doing?

718
01:08:33.120 --> 01:08:36.213
- Four, five, six.
- Hey, stop that.

719
01:08:36.244 --> 01:08:38.192
Seven.

720
01:08:38.233 --> 01:08:41.420
Hey, this is a bad idea.

721
01:08:41.430 --> 01:08:43.607
I believe you said we gonna
do it or die trying.

722
01:08:43.617 --> 01:08:45.554
It's an expression.

723
01:08:45.565 --> 01:08:48.658
Don't think. Jump.

724
01:09:01.301 --> 01:09:03.248
This is really a bad idea.

725
01:09:15.932 --> 01:09:16.942
Come on!

726
01:09:24.170 --> 01:09:27.388
Block the stairs.
Easy enough for men of your size.

727
01:09:44.946 --> 01:09:49.070
- You got a plan?
- Keep our ass, don't get squashed.

728
01:09:52.309 --> 01:09:55.339
I'm going, I'm going.

729
01:09:55.370 --> 01:09:57.516
- On three.
- Three!

730
01:09:58.536 --> 01:10:00.442
Fuck!

731
01:10:04.826 --> 01:10:06.899
Fuck!

732
01:11:27.181 --> 01:11:30.128
What are you doing?
Hurry up!

733
01:11:30.274 --> 01:11:33.148
He's really pissed off!

734
01:11:33.221 --> 01:11:35.512
Hurry!

735
01:12:26.323 --> 01:12:29.645
It's a great future,
you can't forget your past.

736
01:12:29.655 --> 01:12:32.571
I told you Tremaine's all bluff.

737
01:12:37.747 --> 01:12:39.892
No, Tremaine Alexander don't bluff.

738
01:12:39.903 --> 01:12:41.954
Nor do I make a stupid bet.

739
01:12:42.964 --> 01:12:45.183
Untie her.
This game is over.

740
01:12:45.256 --> 01:12:47.265
What are you talking about?

741
01:12:48.140 --> 01:12:51.358
I'm a businessman.
I'm not gonna kill millions of people.

742
01:12:51.410 --> 01:12:54.597
They will come to disarm this thing.

743
01:12:54.607 --> 01:12:57.482
We need to get out of here
before we all get fried.

744
01:12:57.700 --> 01:13:00.679
- You gone soft.
- You watch your tone, woman.

745
01:13:00.720 --> 01:13:03.741
Watch my tone?
What is wrong with you?

746
01:13:03.772 --> 01:13:05.855
Untie the girl!

747
01:13:05.865 --> 01:13:08.073
Maybe I should just kill you
and do this myself.

748
01:13:16.498 --> 01:13:19.403
Who's the bitch now?

749
01:13:41.304 --> 01:13:42.543
Get away from her!

750
01:13:45.407 --> 01:13:46.615
It's okay. It's okay.

751
01:13:46.626 --> 01:13:48.667
I'm so glad you boys
came to save everyone, man.

752
01:13:48.709 --> 01:13:49.771
Not everyone.

753
01:13:51.802 --> 01:13:55.863
Hey, Lino. They're gonna text the code.
You punch it in.

754
01:13:57.050 --> 01:14:00.070
- Now get down on your knees.
- No, wait.

755
01:14:00.206 --> 01:14:02.226
Let him explain.

756
01:14:02.289 --> 01:14:04.371
You want to shoot an unarmed man, Sheriff?

757
01:14:04.382 --> 01:14:07.256
At least you know the shot is coming,
it's better than my father.

758
01:14:07.298 --> 01:14:10.589
- What have i got to do with your father?
- Liutenant John Collier.

759
01:14:11.713 --> 01:14:15.629
- You still blame me for that one?
- You shot him in your headquarters.

760
01:14:15.671 --> 01:14:16.847
Wait.

761
01:14:18.941 --> 01:14:20.878
He never entered the building of mine.

762
01:14:20.888 --> 01:14:22.848
I saw the whole thing from
my surveillance camera.

763
01:14:22.898 --> 01:14:25.220
His own man shot him in the back
and left him for death on my doorstep.

764
01:14:25.231 --> 01:14:26.293
A cold blooded setup.

765
01:14:26.303 --> 01:14:29.251
Your full of shit.
Now get down on your knees.

766
01:14:30.198 --> 01:14:32.302
- Get down on your knees!
- Damien.

767
01:14:32.458 --> 01:14:34.531
- There's a problem.
- What? The number didn't come through?

768
01:14:34.572 --> 01:14:36.645
No, it did.

769
01:14:36.697 --> 01:14:40.821
- 48216.
- That's the code.

770
01:14:40.831 --> 01:14:43.851
- Punch it in.
- It's a setup.

771
01:14:43.955 --> 01:14:46.007
We can't trust those people.

772
01:14:47.121 --> 01:14:50.037
- Punch it in.
- Listen to your man.

773
01:14:50.068 --> 01:14:52.182
They played you for a fool
the way they played your father.

774
01:14:52.193 --> 01:14:53.328
Shut up!

775
01:14:55.463 --> 01:14:57.400
Give me that.

776
01:14:58.514 --> 01:15:01.575
Damien.
Think about it.

777
01:15:01.576 --> 01:15:04.596
- Why is it our ZIP code?
- It's a coincidence.

778
01:15:04.669 --> 01:15:06.814
- Give me the phone.
- My instinct says you'll be arming it.

779
01:15:06.825 --> 01:15:10.813
You're gonna get us all killed.
Give me the phone.

780
01:15:15.021 --> 01:15:17.343
- Lino!
- Sorry partner.

781
01:15:25.549 --> 01:15:27.528
I'm sorry.

782
01:15:27.570 --> 01:15:30.787
Back off.

783
01:15:31.631 --> 01:15:33.849
Stop both of you!

784
01:15:48.554 --> 01:15:51.543
Stay down!

785
01:16:01.894 --> 01:16:04.113
Please! Hurry up!

786
01:16:39.385 --> 01:16:41.468
Damien!

787
01:16:42.520 --> 01:16:44.570
- Collier!
- 20 seconds.

788
01:16:44.571 --> 01:16:48.664
Don't you see?
They told you the van was hijacked.

789
01:16:48.976 --> 01:16:53.080
How come the van had no traces
with that harpoon anywhere on it.

790
01:16:55.100 --> 01:16:59.193
We got 20 seconds to decide
about the rest of life.

791
01:17:01.453 --> 01:17:08.545
Five, four, three, two, one.

792
01:17:11.877 --> 01:17:14.793
Countdown completed.

793
01:17:23.176 --> 01:17:25.280
Jokes on me.

794
01:17:25.290 --> 01:17:29.560
The law never protected this place before.
Why would it start now?

795
01:17:32.591 --> 01:17:35.777
I've done many bad things,
but killing your father wasn't one of them.

796
01:17:47.150 --> 01:17:50.138
I'm making Detroit safer for all.

797
01:17:59.730 --> 01:18:01.875
Welcome to our world.

798
01:18:03.895 --> 01:18:07.009
So, what are we gonna do
with this shit?

799
01:18:14.080 --> 01:18:16.226
Let's give it back.

800
01:18:28.775 --> 01:18:32.878
- For you Captain.
- Thank you son.

801
01:18:49.592 --> 01:18:51.696
- Hold it!
- Let's go!

802
01:18:51.717 --> 01:18:55.872
Hey, come on, no stairs!
Elevator! Let's go, now!

803
01:19:05.266 --> 01:19:08.359
- This is better than the stairs.
- Yeah.

804
01:19:23.990 --> 01:19:25.000
I can't reach him.

805
01:19:25.073 --> 01:19:28.218
We don't have a satellite image.
If the bomb went off, we would've heard it.

806
01:19:28.270 --> 01:19:31.290
I don't like this.
I don't like this at all.

807
01:19:32.228 --> 01:19:34.477
He's our man.
He'll get back to us.

808
01:19:35.498 --> 01:19:36.602
Hello.

809
01:19:37.716 --> 01:19:40.601
What do you mean
they're inside the building?

810
01:19:46.891 --> 01:19:51.046
Hey, you boys remember Lino?
My eyes in Brick Mansions?

811
01:19:52.275 --> 01:19:54.254
Well, he showed me a lot.

812
01:19:56.170 --> 01:19:59.356
Mr. Mayor.
Great place you got here.

813
01:20:05.657 --> 01:20:10.895
Tremaine Alexander.
I'm like the Mayor of Brick Mansions.

814
01:20:10.937 --> 01:20:13.926
It's a pleasure to meet my constituter.

815
01:20:14.165 --> 01:20:19.133
On behalf on myself,
a new appointed Sheriff and Lino

816
01:20:19.143 --> 01:20:22.195
and the citizen of Brick Mansions.

817
01:20:22.236 --> 01:20:26.391
We decided to give you
a campaign contribution.

818
01:20:26.402 --> 01:20:28.506
- Device activated.
- What's going on?

819
01:20:28.516 --> 01:20:30.630
Believe it or not,
I forgot the damn code.

820
01:20:30.672 --> 01:20:33.900
- What was it? 4-8...
- Detective.

821
01:20:33.910 --> 01:20:38.868
- We can take it from here.
- 2-1-6.

822
01:20:38.909 --> 01:20:39.940
Are you sure about that?

823
01:20:39.992 --> 01:20:41.199
I think Lino, you said it couldn't be 6

824
01:20:41.200 --> 01:20:43.148
because that was the ZIP code
for Brick Mansions.

825
01:20:43.189 --> 01:20:45.094
It will be too much of a coincidence?

826
01:20:45.095 --> 01:20:48.313
You said it was a coincidence.
I said they wanted to blow us up.

827
01:20:48.365 --> 01:20:50.573
Yeah, I think all that jumping around
rooftops has us losing it.

828
01:20:50.583 --> 01:20:53.583
You hit your head one too many times.
You're having a hard time to remember.

829
01:20:53.614 --> 01:20:55.551
Gentleman, thank you very
much, we'll take it...

830
01:20:55.593 --> 01:20:57.738
I'm pretty sure the last number is 6.

831
01:20:57.748 --> 01:21:02.777
Mr. Mayor, you want to press the button?
Or does my man Damien have to do it.

832
01:21:02.778 --> 01:21:05.069
- Go for it man.
- Give it a push.

833
01:21:07.163 --> 01:21:10.183
Stop! Stop! Enough!

834
01:21:11.193 --> 01:21:15.286
What the hell happened out there?
You had a direct order.

835
01:21:15.327 --> 01:21:16.567
You played me
just like you played my father.

836
01:21:16.577 --> 01:21:20.534
Yeah, and your empathy made you soft,
just like your father.

837
01:21:20.576 --> 01:21:22.721
I have to make the
tough decision for the city.

838
01:21:22.732 --> 01:21:24.877
And I sent this bomb in there

839
01:21:24.992 --> 01:21:27.866
to get rid of it's problems.

840
01:21:28.012 --> 01:21:31.105
Come on. You know it.

841
01:21:32.115 --> 01:21:34.156
They're no better than animals.

842
01:21:34.260 --> 01:21:38.362
Animals? Who's animals?
Men who struggled to survive?

843
01:21:38.363 --> 01:21:42.560
Or men who will destoy a whole community,
underprivileged women and children?

844
01:21:44.757 --> 01:21:50.942
As a Mayor, I have to do what's best
for all the people of the city.

845
01:21:50.943 --> 01:21:52.891
- The hardworking ones...
- You mean the rich ones?

846
01:21:52.922 --> 01:21:55.067
The ones that contribute.

847
01:21:55.078 --> 01:21:59.180
The ones that are sick and tired
of that cesspool.

848
01:21:59.181 --> 01:22:02.368
Cesspool?
You need to wake up my man.

849
01:22:02.378 --> 01:22:06.294
- The people are rising up.
- And the people...

850
01:22:07.658 --> 01:22:11.543
Check this out.
They're sick of you.

851
01:22:23.123 --> 01:22:26.101
Catch it on the news in about 5 minutes.

852
01:22:41.920 --> 01:22:45.138
The Mayor of Detroit was arrested today
after a compromising video posted online

853
01:22:45.149 --> 01:22:49.106
appeared to show him plotting an attack
on Brick Mansions residence.

854
01:22:49.117 --> 01:22:51.366
"And I sent this bomb in there."

855
01:22:51.408 --> 01:22:54.521
The demolition of walls that divide
the city from the Brick Mansions project

856
01:22:54.532 --> 01:22:56.365
will begin next month.

857
01:22:56.448 --> 01:22:58.426
With no date set for new election,

858
01:22:58.427 --> 01:23:02.551
the acting Mayor announced plans to reopen
schools, hospitals and police stations...

859
01:23:42.385 --> 01:23:45.477
Up, up, up.
That was really good.

860
01:23:45.478 --> 01:23:47.581
Go, go, go.

861
01:23:52.767 --> 01:23:55.954
- Yeah man.
- Yo, Sheriff. What a surprise.

862
01:23:55.965 --> 01:23:58.037
- No more crime to fight around here?
- Yeah.

863
01:23:58.058 --> 01:24:02.983
Well, I see you shared your share of
the reward money very responsibly.

864
01:24:02.984 --> 01:24:04.160
I didn't buy this.
Tremaine gave it to me.

865
01:24:04.202 --> 01:24:05.108
No way.

866
01:24:05.109 --> 01:24:07.118
Yeah, he didn't think it
was right for his image

867
01:24:07.160 --> 01:24:09.232
with the whole
From the People campaign.

868
01:24:09.420 --> 01:24:12.513
- Guys got my vote.
- We're gonna need it.

869
01:24:12.544 --> 01:24:15.595
What about you partner?
I see you still fighting the good fight.

870
01:24:15.606 --> 01:24:18.719
- Only with Lola.
- Lino.

871
01:24:19.802 --> 01:24:22.894
I gotta go, you're making
me uncomfortable.

872
01:24:22.895 --> 01:24:25.041
- Easy partner.
- He's just jealous.

873
01:24:25.051 --> 01:24:28.165
- You guys.
- Hey, on three.

874
01:24:29.050 --> 01:24:31.227
Three.
